+- *The parts PicoMarQ is built from have had security fixes since the versions used here.* `npm audit` lists 19 advisories on 2026-11-22 (12 rated high, 3 moderate, 4 low). Most concern tools that only build the program. Four are in the program: Electron 44.6.0 (fixes through 44.11.5 in the same line), TipTap, ProseMirror's handling of pasted HTML, and KaTeX. PicoMarQ shows no web pages, runs no scripts but its own (`script-src 'self'`), denies new windows, navigation and permission requests, and opens only `http`, `https` and `mailto` links, in the browser. What remains exposed is what a document or pasted text can do to the page engine. A document can also make PicoMarQ fetch a picture from the internet (`![](https://…)`), which tells that server the file was opened. Updating the parts changes the runtime and needs a full test pass, so it is a version of its own.
